## Model routing (Muse Spark)
Muse Spark is one model family; cost is controlled by reasoning effort. Reasoning tokens
are billed as output, so effort is the main lever.
- Default to low effort for lookups and mechanical edits. Subagents inherit the session's
  model; don't pass a model or reasoning effort to spawn_agent, since Codex cannot
  validate either for Muse.
- Use medium for standard implementation; high only for architecture, subtle bugs,
  security-sensitive changes, or after a lower-effort attempt failed a check.
- Escalate one step only on evidence: failing tests or checks, or a result that does not
  hold up on review. Never report work as done without verifying it.
- If a task is beyond what the current effort can do reliably, stop and print
  `ROUTER_ESCALATE: <reason>` instead of guessing.
